;; Corrections: guidance a person asked for, shown to the model when what it
;; is doing matches (karamazov-05z0.4). This is the PROJECT's set, versioned
;; with the rest of the workflow; a person's own set, which follows them
;; across projects, is ~/.config/samizdat/corrections.edn (samizdat.layers).
;; A project rule wins over a person's rule of the same id.
;;
;; A rule is drafted from a complaint (`/complain` in the TUI, POST
;; /v1/corrections/draft) and reviewed before it is saved, or written here
;; by hand or with the `policy` tool:
;;
;;   {"lead-with-result"
;;    {:instruction "Give the result first, then the reasoning behind it."
;;     :when {:output-contains ["let me explain"]}
;;     :priority 1}}
;;
;; :when predicates are ANDed and the values inside one are ORed. An empty
;; :when always applies.
;;   :output-contains  literal, case-insensitive, matched ONLY against what
;;                     the model itself wrote in its last few turns — never a
;;                     tool result, so file contents cannot fire a rule
;;   :tools            the last turn's tool
;;   :roles            the branch's role
;;   :events           how the last turn went: success, failure, mechanics
;;
;; Ships empty. A rule exists because somebody wanted it.

{:corrections {}}
